text:
elaine-sales: Heads-up: NewBridge Commerce wants a 2-week POC. Scope: live receipt streaming -> structured JSON + a function call that enriches SKUs with inventory and margin. They want a tiny drop-in Node example, a webhook sample, and a hosted vs dedicated ballpark for ~60k tokens/day. Any immediate blockers?

nathan-newbridge: Quick notes from their infra: we must propagate request_id, include an example of incremental function payloads, and they want to validate an audit log sample. Latency targets: 180ms for single-item lookup, up to 400ms for full receipt pipeline.

mohit-presales: For hosted POC recommend low-latency mode (disable batching) and a compact model variant. I'll produce a minimal Node streaming + function-call example and a short README on handling chunked tool payloads.

sam-se: Node snippet (streaming + function -> webhook):
```js
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const stream = client.chat.stream({
  model: 'redwood-lite-1',
  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Convert receipt image -> structured JSON' }],
  functions: [{ name: 'enrich_sku', description: 'lookup inventory + margin' }],
  structured_output: { type: 'json_schema', schema: { total: 'number', items: 'array' } }
});
for await (const ev of stream) {
  if (ev.type === 'delta') process.stdout.write(ev.delta);
  if (ev.type === 'function_call') {
    // POST assembled tool payload to their webhook
    await fetch(process.env.WEBHOOK_URL, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ request_id: ev.request_id, payload: ev.payload }) });
  }
}
```

elaine-sales: Perfect. Webhook example they asked for (pseudo):
POST /api/llm-tool-cb
{ "request_id": "req-77f4", "tool": "enrich_sku", "chunks": 3, "chunk_index": 2, "payload": { "sku": "NB-123", "inventory": 42, "margin_pct": 0.31 } }

june-sec: Security checklist: NewBridge requires SOC2, IP allowlist, SAML SSO, and per-request trace IDs. For POC we can use scoped API keys + IP allowlist + short-lived tokens. For production recommend Dedicated or Private with customer-managed KMS and full audit streaming. I'll attach the security one-pager to the invite.

ops-bot: ops-bot: Created infra ticket RDW-9876 to reserve a low-latency hosted slot for the POC. ETA 36h.

mohit-presales: Pricing rough-back-of-envelope: 60k tokens/day -> ~1.8M tokens/mo. Using list hosted price $0.00027/token -> ~ $486/mo. Dedicated reserved pools for consistent 180ms SLOs usually start around $3k/mo depending on GPU profile and region; will get an exact quote and potential discount.

sam-se: Gotcha to call out: function-call outputs can stream across multiple events. Recommend client webhook assemble chunks until a final marker (ev.final === true) or chunk_index==chunks. Also suggest enabling KV cache for repeated receipts and aggressive prefix caching to reduce token regen.

